## Goal

When Tears of the Kwzki Tree's sweep (`radiate_world`, R3569000) turns any card Radiant, `state_check` starts its pass loop over. §4.5 steps 1 to 5 then judge the swept board inside that one check, before the standing evolutions, hand syncs, waiting pairs, deck casts and quests read it. So a base Joro in Defense switches to Attack, and a unit whose Radiant face can't hold its damage dies, in the check that swept them.

The fuzz monitor's I17 also reports any settled unit in Defense Position while it is Indestructible, has Can't Defend or is Evasive, or while an aura bars Defense (`I17 forbidden Defense`). Ruling R3908000 records the decision, with its paragraph in `spec/pending/3908.md`, and the I17 texts say so.

**Departure from the issue (verified by the planner in scratch builds):** through `play` the card test passes on today's engine too. The reason is that `triggers::settle` (`crates/engine/src/triggers.rs` 1666-1675) runs `state_check` again whenever the last one emitted events, and the sweep's `radiantSet` events cause that second run. What is actually wrong today is narrower: one `state_check` call leaves the swept board unjudged and runs its settled steps on it. So the rules tests that fail without the fix call `state_check` once, directly. The Joro card test stays as the end-to-end check through the real card; it passes before and after the change.

